  "title": "Ziyarat of Prophet Isma'il (a.s.), Lady Hajar (s.a.) and the Prophets Buried in the Hijr",
  "data": "In the Hijr Isma'il, beside the Ka'bah, recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى سَيِّدِنَا اِسْمَاعِيْلَ ذَبِيْحِ اللّٰهِ ابْنِ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ خَلِيْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA SAYYIDINAA ISMAA'EELA DHABEEHILLAAHIBNI IBRAAHEEMA KHALEELILLAAH\nPeace be upon our master Isma'il, the one offered in sacrifice to Allah, son of Ibrahim, the Friend of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا نَبِيَّ اللّٰهِ وَابْنَ نَبِيِّهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA NABIYYALLAAHI WABNA NABIYYIH\nPeace be upon you, O Prophet of Allah and son of His Prophet.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَفِيَّ اللّٰهِ وَابْنَ صَفِيِّهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAFIYYALLAAHI WABNA SAFIYYIH\nPeace be upon you, O chosen one of Allah and son of His chosen one.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ اَنْبَعَ اللّٰهُ لَهٗ بِئْرَ زَمْزَمَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN ANBA'ALLAAHU LAHOO BI'RA ZAMZAM\nPeace be upon you, O you for whom Allah made the well of Zamzam spring forth\nحِيْنَ اَسْكَنَهٗ اَبُوْهُ بِوَادٍ غَيْرِ ذِيْ زَرْعٍ عِنْدَ بَيْتِ اللّٰهِ الْمُحَرَّمِ\nHEENA ASKANAHOO ABOOHU BIWAADIN GHAYRI DHEE ZAR'IN I'NDA BAYTILLAAHIL MUHARRAM\nwhen his father settled him in a valley without crops, beside the Sacred House of Allah,\nوَاسْتَجَابَ اللّٰهُ فِيْهِ دَعْوَةَ اَبِيْهِ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ حِيْنَ قَالَ\nWASTAJAABALLAAHU FEEHI DA'WATA ABEEHI IBRAAHEEMA HEENA QAAL\nand Allah answered for him the prayer of his father Ibrahim when he said:\nرَبَّنَا اِنِّيْ اَسْكَنْتُ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِيْ بِوَادٍ غَيْرِ ذِيْ زَرْعٍ عِنْدَ بَيْتِكَ الْمُحَرَّمِ\nRABBANAA INNEE ASKANTU MIN DHURRIYYATEE BIWAADIN GHAYRI DHEE ZAR'IN I'NDA BAYTIKAL MUHARRAM\n\"Our Lord, I have settled some of my offspring in a valley without crops, beside Your Sacred House;\nرَبَّنَا لِيُقِيْمُوا الصَّلَاةَ فَاجْعَلْ اَفْئِدَةً مِنَ النَّاسِ تَهْوِيْ اِلَيْهِمْ\nRABBANAA LIYUQEEMUS SALAATA FAJ'AL AF'IDATAN MINAN NAASI TAHWEE ILAYHIM\nour Lord, that they may establish prayer. So make the hearts of some people incline towards them,\nوَارْزُقْهُمْ مِنَ الثَّمَرَاتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَشْكُرُوْنَ\nWARZUQHUM MINATH THAMARAATI LA'ALLAHUM YASHKUROON\nand provide them with fruits, so that they may be thankful.\"\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ سَلَّمَ نَفْسَهٗ لِلذَّبْحِ طَاعَةً لِاَمْرِ اللّٰهِ تَعَالٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN SALLAMA NAFSAHOO LIDH DHABHI TAA'ATAN LI-AMRILLAAHI TA'AALAA\nPeace be upon you, O you who gave yourself up to be sacrificed, in obedience to the command of Allah, the Exalted,\nاِذْ قَالَ لَهٗ اَبُوْهُ يَا بُنَيَّ اِنِّيْ اَرٰى فِي الْمَنَامِ اَنِّيْ اَذْبَحُكَ فَانْظُرْ مَاذَا تَرٰى\nIDH QAALA LAHOO ABOOHU YAA BUNAYYA INNEE ARAA FIL MANAAMI ANNEE ADHBAHUKA FANZUR MAADHAA TARAA\nwhen his father said to him, \"My son, I see in a dream that I am sacrificing you, so consider what you think.\"\nقَالَ يَا اَبَتِ افْعَلْ مَا تُؤْمَرُ سَتَجِدُنِيْ اِنْ شَاۤءَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ الصَّابِرِيْنَ\nQAALA YAA ABATIF A'L MAA TU'MARU SATAJIDUNEE IN SHAA'ALLAAHU MINAS SAABIREEN\nHe said, \"My father, do as you are commanded; you will find me, if Allah wills, among the patient.\"\nفَدَفَعَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُ الذَّبْحَ وَفَدَاهُ بِذِبْحٍ عَظِيْمٍ\nFADAFA'ALLAAHU A'NHUDH DHABHA WA FADAAHU BIDHIBHIN A'ZEEM\nSo Allah turned the sacrifice away from him and ransomed him with a great sacrifice.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ اَعَانَ اَبَاهُ عَلٰى بِنَاۤءِ الْكَعْبَةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN A'AANA ABAAHU A'LAA BINAA'IL KA'BAH\nPeace be upon you, O you who helped your father build the Ka'bah,\nكَمَا قَالَ اللّٰهُ تَعَالٰى وَاِذْ يَرْفَعُ اِبْرَاهِيْمُ الْقَوَاعِدَ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ وَاِسْمَاعِيْلُ\nKAMAA QAALALLAAHU TA'AALAA WA IDH YARFA'U IBRAAHEEMUL QAWAA'IDA MINAL BAYTI WA ISMAA'EEL\nas Allah, the Exalted, has said: \"And when Ibrahim was raising the foundations of the House, and Isma'il with him:\nرَبَّنَا تَقَبَّلْ مِنَّا اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ\nRABBANAA TAQABBAL MINNAA INNAKA ANTAS SAMEE'UL A'LEEM\n'Our Lord, accept it from us; You are the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.'\"\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ مَدَحَهُ اللّٰهُ تَعَالٰى فِيْ كِتَابِهٖ بِقَوْلِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN MADAHAHULLAAHU TA'AALAA FEE KITAABIHEE BIQAWLIH\nPeace be upon you, O you whom Allah, the Exalted, praised in His Book, saying:\nوَاذْكُرْ فِي الْكِتَابِ اِسْمَاعِيْلَ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ صَادِقَ الْوَعْدِ وَكَانَ رَسُوْلًا نَبِيًّا\nWADHKUR FIL KITAABI ISMAA'EELA INNAHOO KAANA SAADIQAL WA'DI WA KAANA RASOOLAN NABIYYAA\n\"And mention Isma'il in the Book; he was true to his promise, and he was a messenger and a prophet.\nوَكَانَ يَاْمُرُ اَهْلَهٗ بِالصَّلَاةِ وَالزَّكَاةِ وَكَانَ عِنْدَ رَبِّهٖ مَرْضِيًّا\nWA KAANA YA'MURU AHLAHOO BIS SALAATI WAZ ZAKAATI WA KAANA I'NDA RABBIHEE MARDIYYAA\nHe enjoined prayer and charity on his family, and his Lord was pleased with him.\"\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ جَعَلَ اللّٰهُ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِهٖ مُحَمَّدًا سَيِّدَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ وَخَاتَمَ النَّبِيِّيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN JA'ALALLAAHU MIN DHURRIYYATIHEE MUHAMMADAN SAYYIDAL MURSALEENA WA KHAATAMAN NABIYYEEN\nPeace be upon you, O you among whose descendants Allah placed Muhammad, the master of the messengers and the seal of the prophets,\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE WA SALLAM\nAllah bless him and his family and grant them peace.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰى اَبِيْكَ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ خَلِيْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA WA A'LAA ABEEKA IBRAAHEEMA KHALEELILLAAH\nPeace be upon you and upon your father Ibrahim, the Friend of Allah,\nوَعَلٰى اَخِيْكَ اِسْحَاقَ نَبِيِّ اللّٰهِ\nWA A'LAA AKHEEKA IS-HAAQA NABIYYILLAAH\nand upon your brother Ishaq, the Prophet of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰى جَمِيْعِ اَنْبِيَاۤءِ اللّٰهِ الْمَدْفُوْنِيْنَ بِهٰذِهِ الْبُقْعَةِ الْمُبَارَكَةِ الْمُعَظَّمَةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA WA A'LAA JAMEE'I ANBIYAA'ILLAAHIL MADFOONEENA BIHAADHIHIL BUQ'ATIL MUBAARAKATIL MU'AZZAMAH\nPeace be upon you and upon all the prophets of Allah buried in this blessed and honoured ground.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰى اُمِّكَ الطَّاهِرَةِ الصَّابِرَةِ هَاجَرَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA WA A'LAA UMMIKAT TAAHIRATIS SAABIRATI HAAJARA WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon you and upon your pure and patient mother, Hajar, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nحَشَرَنَا اللّٰهُ فِيْ زُمْرَتِكُمْ تَحْتَ لِوَاۤءِ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ\nHASHARANALLAAHU FEE ZUMRATIKUM TAHTA LIWAA'I MUHAMMADIN SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE WA SALLAM\nMay Allah raise us in your company beneath the banner of Muhammad, Allah bless him and his family and grant them peace,\nوَلَا جَعَلَهُ اللّٰهُ اٰخِرَ الْعَهْدِ مِنْ زِيَارَتِكُمْ\nWA LAA JA'ALAHULLAAHU AAKHIRAL A'HDI MIN ZIYAARATIKUM\nand may Allah not make this my last visit to you.\nوَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWAS SALAAMU A'LAYKUM WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAnd peace be upon you all, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nThen pray two rak'ahs of ziyarat there and offer their reward to him.",
  "merits": "Prophet Isma'il (a.s.), son of Ibrahim (a.s.), and his mother Hajar are buried, by narration, in the Hijr Isma'il, the semicircular enclosure on the north side of the Ka'bah. Al-Halabi asked Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) about the Hijr; the Imam said that Isma'il buried his mother there and, disliking that her grave be walked on, walled it in, and that the graves of prophets are in it (al-Kafi).\n\nThis ziyarat is given in the Shia manuals of Hajj, such as Sayyid Jawad Husayni Shahrudi's Adab al-Haramayn, which cite no narration for it. The manuals add that after the two rak'ahs one may pray for whatever one wishes."
}
